   {
    "id": "t1",
    "start": 0.0,
    "end": 5.52,
    "text": "Try this easy hack for your anxiety. Do you ever crave salty foods when you are stressed out and"
   },
   {
    "id": "t2",
    "start": 5.52,
    "end": 11.12,
    "text": "you're very anxious? Well that's because your brain has very specific sensors for sodium and this"
   },
   {
    "id": "t3",
    "start": 11.12,
    "end": 16.88,
    "text": "is going to help to maintain your homeostasis and of course the balance between your fight or flight,"
   },
   {
    "id": "t4",
    "start": 16.88,
    "end": 21.44,
    "text": "your sympathetic nervous system and your parasympathetic. So my tip here, just get a little bit"
   },
   {
    "id": "t5",
    "start": 21.44,
    "end": 27.68,
    "text": "of salt and put a pinch into your mouth, ideally under your tongue and drink that down with a little"
   },
   {
    "id": "t6",
    "start": 27.68,
    "end": 31.68,
    "text": "bit of water. You can do this throughout the day when you are feeling anxious to help to balance"
   },
   {
    "id": "t7",
    "start": 31.68,
    "end": 36.08,
    "text": "those electrolytes and maintaining your other electrolytes as well. So magnesium is going to"
   },
   {
    "id": "t8",
    "start": 36.08,
    "end": 41.6,
    "text": "be really important for your nervous system and other herbal medicines that I love for anxiety."
   },
   {
    "id": "t9",
    "start": 41.6,
    "end": 46.8,
    "text": "So things like valerian, skull cat, passion flower, and lemon balm, that combination together is"
   },
   {
    "id": "t10",
    "start": 46.8,
    "end": 51.04,
    "text": "amazing for chronic anxiety. Follow for more natural health tips."
   }
  ]
 },
